or Masterson's debate absences becoming a bigger story, could tighten this into true tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Laura Kelly (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kansas is holding an open governor's race now that Laura Kelly's tenure has ended, with Democrat Cindy Holscher facing Senate President Ty Masterson. The state's Republican lean gives Masterson a structural advantage, and recent surveys from Emerson, co/efficient, and Wedgewood all show him ahead, with independent voters reportedly fueling his lead. Most expert raters call the race Lean R for a flip, though RealClearPolitics still lists it a Tossup.\n\nHolscher, a Johnson County moderate, has tried to make the race a referendum on Masterson's record, attacking him for skipping debates and pressing on property taxes and data center regulation. Markets give her roughly a three-in-ten chance. The race remains within reach if she consolidates moderates, but the weight of the evidence favors Masterson by mid-single digits.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1817, "margin": -4.47}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.161, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1643, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1648, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1797, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1739, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.215, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2315, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2051, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2039, "margin": -4.5}]}